From f5134cf6dfa6a6afbbc25060c4bdd8df9b27e59a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zahary Karadjov <zahary.karadjov@metacraft-labs.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 11:11:46 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Don't let instances stuck in deletion fill a pool

Every instance row counted against max_runners, including the ones on
the deletion lane (pending_delete, pending_force_delete, deleting). Those
are already gone from the forge and can never take a job; they only wait
for the provider to confirm the teardown. When a provider's deletes stall
for hours, a pool of N runners ends up with N rows being deleted and no
usable runner, and every queued job gets "max workers reached".

Add internal/capacity, which decides which instances occupy a slot:
deleted never counts; instances on the deletion lane do not count, up to
max_runners of them; any beyond that do. The bound keeps a pool whose
deletes never succeed at 2 x max_runners instances on the provider.

Use it in addRunnerToPool(), ensureIdleRunnersForOnePool() (which also
stops counting a deleting instance as idle), the transactional check in
CreateInstance(), and the scale set worker's runnerCount(). The scale
set's handleScaleDown() computes its delta from live runners only, so
deleting runners beyond the allowance never cause idle runners to be
removed.

Signed-off-by: Zahary Karadjov <zahary.karadjov@metacraft-labs.com>
